      "dynamicRanges": ["sdr"],
      "requiresGpu": true,
      "notes": "Smooth motion (FL-162). The weights come from the Frameleaf model source (frameleaf/rife-4.25); `python -m frameleaf_ml.video_restoration fetch-weights rife-4-25` downloads them once the sha256 is pinned. frameleaf_interpolate.py is the runtime's frame-folder entry point and must be confirmed against the pinned commit. requiresGpu false is only for a record qualified on the processor. Every REPLACE value and every limit must come from the qualification run."
    },
    {
      "id": "codeformer-photo-repair",
      "family": "codeformer",
      "operation": "repair",
      "displayName": "Photo repair (CodeFormer and LaMa)",
      "repository": "https://github.com/sczhou/CodeFormer",
      "revision": "REPLACE-with-the-exact-40-character-commit-that-was-qualified",
      "license": {
        "code": "NTU S-Lab License 1.0",
        "weights": "NTU S-Lab License 1.0 (CodeFormer); MIT (RetinaFace detection, ParseNet parsing); Apache-2.0 (LaMa)",
        "url": "https://github.com/sczhou/CodeFormer/blob/master/LICENSE"
      },
      "nativeScale": null,
      "runtime": {
        "root": "/opt/restoration/codeformer",
        "python": "/opt/restoration/photo/.venv/bin/python",
        "argv": [
          "{python}",
          "-I",
          "/usr/src/video-restoration/runtimes/photo_repair.py",
          "--input-dir",
          "{input_dir}",
          "--output-dir",
          "{output_dir}",
          "--runtime-root",
          "{runtime_root}",
          "--codeformer",
          "{weight:codeformer}",
          "--detection",
          "{weight:detection}",
          "--parsing",
          "{weight:parsing}",
          "--lama",
          "{weight:lama}",
          "--fidelity",
          "0.7"
        ],
        "env": {},
        "timeoutSeconds": 900
      },
      "weights": [
        {
          "role": "codeformer",
          "path": "codeformer/codeformer.pth",
          "sha256": "REPLACE-with-the-sha256-measured-during-qualification",
          "source": { "repo": "codeformer", "file": "codeformer.pth" }
        },
        {
          "role": "detection",
          "path": "codeformer/detection_Resnet50_Final.pth",
          "sha256": "REPLACE-with-the-sha256-measured-during-qualification",
          "source": { "repo": "retinaface-resnet50", "file": "detection_Resnet50_Final.pth" }
        },
        {
          "role": "parsing",
          "path": "codeformer/parsing_parsenet.pth",
          "sha256": "REPLACE-with-the-sha256-measured-during-qualification",
          "source": { "repo": "parsenet", "file": "parsing_parsenet.pth" }
        },
        {
          "role": "lama",
          "path": "lama/model.onnx",
          "sha256": "REPLACE-with-the-sha256-measured-during-qualification",
          "source": { "repo": "frameleaf-inpaint", "file": "visual/model.onnx" }
        }
      ],
      "limits": {
        "maxInputLongEdge": 8192,
        "maxFrames": 1,
        "maxFramesPerChunk": 1,
        "minVramBytes": 0
      },
      "dynamicRanges": ["sdr"],
      "requiresGpu": true,
      "notes": "Photo repair (FL-933), stills only. An 8-bit photo up to 8192 px on its long edge (67 megapixels; a 600 dpi scan of an 8 x 10 inch print is 4800 x 6000) comes back at exactly its own size. Faces are found on a copy of at most 1536 px and restored at 512 x 512 with fidelity 0.7; a face wider than about 2048 px, or with eyes under 10 px apart, is left as it is. Scratches and dust are filled in 512 px windows, never inside a face, and the pass is skipped when the marks cover more than 3% of the photo. The weights come from the Frameleaf model source (frameleaf/codeformer, frameleaf/retinaface-resnet50, frameleaf/parsenet, frameleaf/frameleaf-inpaint); `python -m frameleaf_ml.video_restoration fetch-weights codeformer-photo-repair` downloads them once each sha256 is pinned. A qualified NVIDIA GPU is required; requiresGpu false is refused. Every REPLACE value and minVramBytes must come from the qualification run."
    },
