        }
      ],
      "limits": {
        "maxInputLongEdge": 8192,
        "maxFrames": 1,
        "maxFramesPerChunk": 1,
        "minVramBytes": 0
      },
      "dynamicRanges": ["sdr"],
      "requiresGpu": true,
      "notes": "Colourise (FL-933), stills only: the DDColor large (ConvNeXt-L) model trained with the ModelScope data cleaning. An 8-bit photo up to 8192 px on its long edge comes back at exactly its own size: the model sees a 512 x 512 copy and its two colour channels are enlarged and joined to the photo's own full-size lightness, so GPU memory does not grow with the scan. The weights come from the Frameleaf model source (frameleaf/ddcolor); `python -m frameleaf_ml.video_restoration fetch-weights ddcolor-colourise` downloads them once the sha256 is pinned. A qualified NVIDIA GPU is required; requiresGpu false is refused. Every REPLACE value and minVramBytes must come from the qualification run."
